# Domoticz-Rainstats: technical settings.
#
# Copy this file to ".env" in the same directory as plugin.py and remove the "#" of the lines you want to change
# (the lines that start with RS_LAST_ are not commented: change Y to N there). Everything is optional: without a .env
# the plugin uses the values shown here. Changes take effect when the
# hardware is restarted (Setup > Hardware > the plugin > Update, or restart Domoticz). A variable of the same name in
# the environment of the Domoticz service wins over this file. A mistyped name is reported in the Domoticz log.
# The settings of the hardware page (address, IDX of the rain device, interval, ...) are not repeated here.

# How the Domoticz JSON API is reached: http or https. Certificates are always verified.
# RS_SCHEME=http

# A certificate authority file (PEM) to trust in addition to the public ones, for https with your own CA.
# RS_CA_FILE=

# Seconds to wait for an answer of Domoticz (3-60).
# RS_HTTP_TIMEOUT=10

# Where the archive is kept. Default: rainstats_state.json beside plugin.py. A deployment (deploy.sh) never touches it.
# RS_STATE_FILE=

# The state file is written at most this often, in seconds (60-86400), and always when the plugin stops. At most this
# much of the rain data can be lost when Domoticz is killed without a clean stop.
# RS_SAVE_INTERVAL=900

# Rewrite an unchanged value this often, in seconds (30-86400), so that Domoticz' sensor time-out never marks a quiet
# sensor as dead.
# RS_REFRESH_INTERVAL=300

# Divide the RainRate of the rain device by this number (1-1000). Domoticz' JSON API answers mm/h, so 1 is right. Use
# 100 only if the rate you see here is 100 times too high.
# RS_RATE_DIVISOR=1

# More rain than this (mm, 1-1000) between two readings is taken for a sensor error: nothing is counted and the new
# value becomes the baseline.
# RS_MAX_DELTA=100

# The data file of the dzVents script "RainStats V2.6" (rain_stats_data.json). It is imported ONCE, when the plugin
# starts for the first time (no state file yet); the script's file is never changed. Remove the line afterwards, or leave
# it: it is ignored as soon as a state file exists.
# RS_LEGACY_FILE=/path/to/rain_stats_data.json

# The IDX of a Domoticz rain device whose DAILY RAIN HISTORY is read ONCE (the "Last year" graph of Domoticz), to fill
# the days before the plugin started: with it the long windows are complete from the first day. It can be the rain
# device of the hardware page or another one. The days the plugin collected itself are never overwritten, the
# history is spread evenly over each day (it has no hours) and has no rain rates. When it was read, the state file
# says so and the device is never asked again; only a deleted state file brings the import back. Check what
# Domoticz would answer first: python3 -m rain_stats --history <IDX>
# RS_HISTORY_IDX=1161

# Which windows get devices. Y = the plugin creates "Rain <N> d" (and, unless the hardware setting Statistics is
# "Rain only", "Peak Rain Rate <N> d") and keeps it up to date; N = it does not. The first eight are Y (the windows of
# the first version), the others N. Changes take effect when the hardware is restarted. A device that exists already is
# not deleted when you set N: it stays where it is and is no longer updated; delete it in Domoticz when you do not
# want it any more. At least one window must be Y.
RS_LAST_001_DAYS=Y
RS_LAST_002_DAYS=Y
RS_LAST_007_DAYS=Y
RS_LAST_014_DAYS=Y
RS_LAST_024_DAYS=N
RS_LAST_030_DAYS=Y
RS_LAST_060_DAYS=N
RS_LAST_090_DAYS=Y
RS_LAST_120_DAYS=N
RS_LAST_180_DAYS=Y
RS_LAST_360_DAYS=N
RS_LAST_365_DAYS=Y
